From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:21:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: map the whole PMP SRAM

The PMP node maps 0x80000 bytes of the PMP's SRAM at 0x380500000. The ADT
lists 0xc0000 there (J604: /arm-io/pmp reg[2]), and the firmware's __DATA
segment ends at 0xa5000 (/arm-io/pmp segment-ranges[1]), past the
mapping. A deep sleep has to keep that segment, so map all of it.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
index da81240f36..61556392c9 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
@@ -1144,7 +1144,7 @@
 
 	pmp: pmp@380500000 {
 		compatible = "apple,t8132-pmp-v2", "apple,t6000-pmp-v2";
-		reg = <0x3 0x80500000 0x0 0x80000>,
+		reg = <0x3 0x80500000 0x0 0xc0000>,
 		      <0x3 0x80e00000 0x0 0x4000>;
 		reg-names = "pmp", "asc";
 		mboxes = <&pmp_mbox>;
-- 
2.43.0

